    "body": "LOGICAL_OWNER = JINGO\nROLE = SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE / REFERENCE TRANSPORT\nSTATE = DESIGN GATE APPROVED / ARCHITECTURE RESEARCH AUTHORIZED\nOWNER_DECISION = APPROVE ZORR REFERENCE BRIDGE V1 DESIGN GATE\nINHERITS = #73 umbrella; #76 Studio Constitution R02\nDAEMON_BASE = Controller Daemon v1 PRODUCTION ACTIVE exact 9e2ccfbaca88a95eac2e119e5eac720f9074dd35\n\n## PURPOSE\nRemove manual copying of reference images into `D:\\BLATT2\\ZB_AGENT_INBOX\\<TASK_ID>\\` while preserving exact task binding, source integrity, authority boundaries, and fail-closed behavior.\n\n## HARD BOUNDARIES\n- DESIGN/FEASIBILITY ONLY. No implementation is authorized by this gate.\n- Do not modify Controller Daemon v1 production code/runtime/profile.\n- Do not modify SALVADOR model/workflow/prompt/denoise/dimensions.\n- No canon mutation or automatic promotion.\n- No ComfyUI lifecycle changes.\n- No Babylon integration.\n- No paid API/service requirement.\n- `REFERENCE ARRIVAL != TASK AUTHORITY`.\n- `FILE PRESENT != FILE TRUSTED`.\n- `UNKNOWN TASK_ID -> QUARANTINE / STOP`.\n- `HASH MISMATCH -> STOP`.\n- `DUPLICATE/CONFLICT -> STOP`.\n\n## REQUIRED DESIGN QUESTIONS\n1. What transport is the v1 authority: Google Drive sync, GitHub attachment/download, or local companion/drop UI?\n2. How is `TASK_ID` cryptographically/logically bound to the delivered file?\n3. What manifest accompanies each delivery: filename, size, SHA256, MIME/type, source status, task id, created-at, transport id?\n4. How are duplicate/replayed/late files handled?\n5. How does the local bridge stage -> verify -> atomically publish into `ZB_AGENT_INBOX\\<TASK_ID>`?\n6. How are partial-sync files prevented from being consumed?\n7. What is the failure/quarantine location and durable GitHub evidence?\n8. What permissions/security assumptions exist for the transport folder/account?\n9. How does the design avoid making Google Drive or any transport a canon/task-state authority?\n\n## CANDIDATE APPROACHES TO EVALUATE\nA. Google Drive Drop -> Drive Desktop/local sync -> validated local bridge -> inbox.\nB. GitHub issue attachment -> local authenticated downloader -> validated local bridge -> inbox.\nC. Local companion/drop UI -> validated local bridge -> inbox.\n\nNo approach is selected yet.\n\n## KNOWN CONNECTOR FACTS\nThe connected Google Drive surface can create folders, search/list folders, and upload connector file references. No existing `ZORR` Drive folder was found during gate opening. Local Google Drive Desktop presence/sync state on owner-PC is NOT YET VERIFIED.\n\n## SUCCESS CRITERIA FOR DESIGN\n- zero manual file copy for normal reference delivery;\n- exact TASK_ID binding;\n- byte integrity via SHA256;\n- atomic local publish only after full validation;\n- duplicates/replays/conflicts fail closed;\n- transport outage cannot fabricate task state;\n- existing Controller Daemon consumes only validated inbox files;\n- one disposable owner-PC end-to-end smoke defined before production activation;\n- explicit owner approval of written spec before implementation planning.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION = NOT AUTHORIZED\nREFERENCE_BRIDGE_PRODUCTION = NO\nNEXT = JINGO context questions -> 2-3 approaches -> recommended design -> written spec -> OWNER spec review.",
